==English==

===Etymology 1===
Attested since 1822; from {{bor|en|sco|yank}}. {{unk|en}} origin.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/ˈjæŋk/|[ˈjæŋk]|a=non-æ-tensing}}
** {{audio|en|En-au-yank.ogg|a=AU}}
* {{a|en|æ-tensing}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈjeɪ̯ŋk/|[ˈjeɪ̯ŋk]|;|/ˈjɛ̃ŋk/|[ˈjɛ̃ŋk]|a=US,CA}}
* {{rhymes|en|æŋk|s=1}}
* {{hyph|en|yank}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[sudden]], [[vigorous]] [[pull]] (sometimes defined as mass times [[jerk]], or rate of change of [[force]]).
#: {{syn|en|jerk|tug}}
#: {{ux|en|He unjammed the rope with a short '''yank'''.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} An act of [[masturbation]].
#: {{syn|en|fap|wank|Thesaurus:masturbation}}
# {{senseid|en|stabber}}{{lb|en|slang|MLE}} {{alt form|en|shank|id=stabber|t=stabbing weapon}}.
# {{lb|en|physics|engineering}} The rate of [[change]] in [[force]] with respect to [[time]].

