====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[pull]] (something) with a [[quick]], [[strong]] [[action]].
#: {{syn|en|jerk|tug}}
#* {{RQ:Wired|year=2016|month=October|title=Barack Obama Talks AI, Robo Cars, and the Future of the World|quotee=Barack Obama|author=Scott Dadich|url=https://www.wired.com/2016/10/president-obama-mit-joi-ito-interview/|passage=[Regarding risks of AI] And you just have to have somebody close to the power cord. [Laughs.]{{sic}} Right when you see it about to happen, you gotta '''yank''' that electricity out of the wall, man.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261012075542/https://www.wired.com/2016/10/president-obama-mit-joi-ito-interview/|archivedate=12 October 2026}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|informal}} To [[remove]]; to [[recall]] or [[revoke]].
#: {{syn|en|pull}}
#: {{ux|en|They '''yanked''' the product as soon as they learned it was unsafe.}}
#: {{ux|en|The cops '''yanked''' my driver's license.}}
# {{lb|en|ambitransitive|slang}} To [[masturbate]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:masturbate}}

